WEBVTT

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:28.850
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:28.850
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:28.850
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:54.430 --> 00:02:02.850
The 3rd Battle of Tiamat

00:01:54.430 --> 00:02:02.850
Part I

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:09.250
Near the end of Space
Year 794, Imperial Year 485...

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:12.910
...an expedition was being 
approved in the Galactic Empire.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:19.250
So just for the sake of embellishing the 30th anniversary of His Majesty's enthronement...

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.500
...you're saying that we
must launch an expedition ?

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:27.940
Kaiser Friedrich IV's reign was reaching
30 years at New Year's, a rare achievement.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:31.320
However, his accomplishments in
domestic affairs were close to nonexistent.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:38.750
It's normal for a ruler to divert attention 
from that fact with external military activities.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:41.700
But, Chief Commander,
it's also true that recently...

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:46.110
...the rebels have been continuously launching attacks against us.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:50.420
That last time was the sixth time
they attacked Iserlohn Fortress.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.680
We repelled them there...

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:59.680
...and before that, we went as far as Vanfleet
Starzone to destroy a rebel front-line base.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:06.050
But two years ago, we almost lost
Iserlohn Fortress, and going back further...

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:10.200
...we suffered a devastating loss in
a battle in Arlesheim Starzone.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.600
It's not that I'm blaming only you.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.450
We all share the same accountability.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:25.900
It's about time to deal painful retribution 
to the rebels and accomplish something.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:27.280
That's all there is to it.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:30.300
Even if Fleet Admiral Muckenberger had any complaints...

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.250
...it wasn't like the 
decision would be reversed.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:36.200
After the New Year, in 
January of Imperial Year 486...

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:43.100
...the Empire was about to launch a fleet of
35,400 ships, with the Kaiser in attendance.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:46.220
Of course, there were many who 
welcomed the decision on the expedition.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:50.750
Reinhard von Musel was
also pleased with the decision.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:58.260
Right after I become a Vice Admiral and am given command of a fleet this expedition comes along.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.320
Good fortune is coming my way.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.010
Look at Muckenberger.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.500
He looks so dignified.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:10.770
But of course,
he merely looks dignified.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:23.920
The news of an impending Imperial attack had
already reached the Alliance via Phezzan.

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:31.670
The Alliance immediately deployed patrol units
to the space zone outside Iserlohn Corridor...

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.670
...but a problem arose at that time.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.300
Because of errors in 
supply ship deployment...

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:42.010
...a shortage of daily necessities and fuel became grave for the front-line fleet.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.700
The military was not able to take
care of the problem on its own...

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:49.350
...so about 100 civilian ships were hired
from nearby zones to deliver the supplies.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.010
Of course we'll be 
sending along naval escorts.

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:54.880
I've arranged for cruisers and destroyers, totaling 10 ships.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:59.240
That's fine, but military ships are
valuable, especially before a battle...

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:04.410
...so be sure to warn them not to take
risky actions that could endanger them.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:05.950
Yes, sir.

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:09.940
Even though he didn't tell them
to abandon their duty as escorts...

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:14.920
...it's also true that Lobos's instruction significantly diminished the escorts' sense of responsibility...

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:19.250
...and many of them turned back before
entering the dangerous space area.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:22.340
Captain, the naval escorts are 
turning back one after another.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:26.290
This is why military people
are difficult to deal with.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:30.360
Doesn't the military exist in order
to protect the people's safety ?

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:34.300
But they're abandoning their escort 
duty for the sake of their own safety...

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.600
...and it really ought
to be the reverse.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:37.790
What should we do ?

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:39.250
Should we turn back, too ?

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.400
We're proud merchants.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.100
We take responsibility 
for the business we do.

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:47.400
Our mentality is different
from those servicemen.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.970
But one cruiser remained there.

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:54.050
It was a cruiser named Grand Canal.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:59.550
When its consorts turned back in an excessive reaction to Fleet Admiral Lobos's directive...

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:04.000
...this one ship dutifully stayed there to fulfill its initial orders to accompany the civilian ships.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.600
On the third day...

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:11.940
...they encountered Imperial cruisers roaming
the area, as if they were hunting for prey.

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:15.350
The cruisers were evenly
matched in battle capability.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:18.700
Therefore, in a battle of 1-on-2, the win-loss
outcome was obvious from the beginning.

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:23.250
For that reason, Grand Canal sacrificed
itself in order to buy time with all its might...

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:25.500
...so that the civilian
ships could get away.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:29.450
But it wasn't a battle, but
rather a one-sided massacre.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:33.700
Among the ones slow to escape, one ship
was sunk, and another was captured...

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:36.200
...but half of the others
reached their destination...

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:40.350
...and the others were able
to reach the safety zone.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:44.300
Grand Canal not only saved
the lives of the civilians...

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.960
...but also the honor 
of the Alliance military.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:51.400
The military gave Captain Fegan and all the other casualties Freedom Fighter Medals...

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:53.900
...and commended 
their accomplishments.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:57.300
It cannot be denied that by spotlighting
their good deeds as a laudable anecdote...

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.650
...they intended to divert attention from 
the other ships that abandoned their duty...

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:04.300
...and avoid criticism against the commanding officer who had sent the directive in question.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:05.650
Admiral, Admiral...{inaudible}

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:10.410
Admiral Holland, what do you
think of this Grand Canal affair ?

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:14.900
There's been criticism that the commanding officer was stingy with naval escorts, but...

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:17.730
Only people who are ignorant about
military affairs would say such things.

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:21.540
In preparation for an important battle, we 
must have as many ships as we can gather...

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:25.040
...and we can't afford to
lose them in skirmishes.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:33.110
We saved nine ships with the sacrifice of one ship so Fleet Admiral Lobos's directive was correct.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:36.170
Their sacrifice wasn't meaningless -
is that what you're saying ?

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:38.040
Exactly.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:41.560
The front line received the supplies,
and the morale of the military has risen.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:47.700
Preventing the expected Imperial encroachment and expanding Alliance territory instead...

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:51.700
...that's how we can reward
the souls of those war heroes.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:54.850
This time the 11th Fleet
will be mobilized...

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:57.550
...so what are your thoughts on 
commanding a fleet for the first time ?

00:07:57.550 --> 00:07:59.700
Being a Vice Admiral
at the age of 32...

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:03.460
...was a feat accomplished only by Admiral Bruce Ashbey, but what do you think ?

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:06.650
There are people who say that you're the return of Admiral Ashbey, but...{what are your thoughts}?

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:07.880
I'm flattered.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.250
In this battle, we'll emulate
Admiral Ashbey's historic deeds...

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:12.700
...and intercept the Imperial forces
in the Tiamat Starzone.

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:16.800
I will thoroughly annihilate
them with my tactics !

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:22.850
Commodore Yang, can
you tell us your thoughts ?

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:32.250
Like the Hero of El Facil,
Grand Canal saved civilians...

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:35.780
...so what do you think of their
awarding of medals today ?

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:43.200
Um, Grand Canal probably needed another friendly ship, instead of 100 medals.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.350
Please conduct interviews 
only through official channels.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:47.730
Other comments should
not be put in articles.

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.150
Commodore, please come this way.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.030
One year earlier, Yang had
been promoted to commodore...

00:08:57.030 --> 00:09:02.320
...in recognition of the operational proposals he made at the Battle of Vanfleet Starzone.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:06.200
The 28 year old commodore 
was a hero to the mass media...

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:09.250
...but his words and action were heresy to the eyes of the military mainstream...

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:11.150
...and were always kept in check.

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:22.000
In February, the Alliance forces
decided on a final operational plan.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:26.700
The plan declared in front of the media by
11th Fleet Commander, Vice Admiral Holland...

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:30.640
...to intercept the enemy in the Tiamat Starzone was essentially approved.

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:35.700
And since there aren't many
starzones suited for interception...

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:39.050
...it was a plan with a 
high probability of action...

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:41.110
...so that was part of the reason
there were few dissenting voices.

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:45.990
But what moved Fleet Admiral Lobos to his final decision might have been Holland's words...

00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:50.660
...that they would replicate the total
victory of Fleet Admiral Bruce Ashbey.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:54.690
Five fleets were to be mobilized.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:59.300
In addition to Holland's 11th Fleet, the vanguard, as advised by Vice Admiral Sitolet...

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:04.010
...also included Vice Admiral Bucock's 5th Fleet and Vice Admiral Ulanfu's 10th Fleet.

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:06.700
And once the Ministry
of Defense approved...

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:09.050
...the 4th Fleet, led
by Vice Admiral Pastoll...

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:12.300
...and the 6th Fleet, led by 
Vice Admiral Moore, were to be added.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:13.700
On the other hand...

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:18.890
...the Imperial forces had already reached
Iserlohn Fortress and were being resupplied.

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:21.910
Did you hear, Kircheis ?

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:24.050
It seems Fortress 
Commander Stockhausen...

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:29.200
...and Fortress Resident Fleet Commander Seeckt have quarreled yet again.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:30.380
Again ?

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:33.670
Moreover, they did it in front
of the Chief Commander.

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:37.320
And I heard Muckenberger
was forced to intervene.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:41.400
It would've been interesting to see how he
maintained his dignity while separating them.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:44.410
Lord Reinhard, you're evil.

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:45.750
Don't say that.

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:47.850
By the way, did you have
something to tell me ?

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:52.420
A meeting will be held shortly on the flagship of said Fleet Admiral Muckenberger.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.300
Please prepare.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.700
Yeah, that reminds me.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.320
Did you forget about it ?

00:10:58.320 --> 00:10:59.810
I didn't forget it.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:01.290
It's just I wanted to forget
about this present situation...

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:05.950
...that still has me at the beck and call of these people.

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:07.230
Lord Reinhard.

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:12.000
Ever since the incompetent Grand
Duke Helbert lost at Dagon Starzone...

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.150
...how many battles do you
think have taken place ?

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:14.960
I haven't a clue.

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:18.010
Including skirmishes,
there have been 329 of them.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:21.080
329 times in 150 years.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:23.500
I wonder how they managed to keep it up without getting bored with it.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.990
The war didn't come to an end, so...

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:30.950
The Alliance, no, the rebel forces
don't have a clue about strategy.

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:35.350
That there's a way to neutralize Iserlohn Fortress without any bloodshed.

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:40.110
To begin with, why are they so
ridiculously obsessed with Iserlohn ?

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:44.250
They believe that if there is a fortress, they
have to attack from the front and besiege it.

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:47.250
That's the extreme of
rigid thought processes.

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:52.600
That's why it was important for the Empire to have built the fortress.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:54.230
That's right.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:56.510
But in any case, it's about time.

00:11:56.510 --> 00:12:00.560
Your shuttle has already been prepared, and Rear Admiral Nolden is waiting.

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:01.800
I don't want to go.

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:05.440
Even if I go, it's not like
they'll listen to my input.

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:10.700
I'm used to alienation and antagonism, but I can't stand spending fruitless time alone.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:14.150
Kircheis, if you were coming
with me, that would be a comfort...

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:16.730
...but the Chief Staff Officer
is accompanying me, so...

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:19.200
Do you dislike 
Rear Admiral Nolden ?

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.110
It's not a matter of like or dislike.

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:22.590
He's useless.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:24.500
He's a Rear Admiral at the age of 32.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:26.500
There could be more
to him than you think.

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:30.160
He's getting promoted quickly only
because he's the scion of a viscount family.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:34.350
When I see him, I realize that the military is just another bureaucratic structure.

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:40.080
I sense the personnel department's
malice in assigning that moron to me.

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:43.520
I think they're just not
being thoughtful enough.

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:45.790
But in any case, Lord Reinhard...

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:51.800
If I attend, the average age of the participants will get lower.

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:53.430
That's the only saving grace.

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:57.200
Without acknowledging
the enemy's surrender...

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:02.350
...we will completely destroy them and 
make the glory of our Kaiser known to all.

00:13:02.350 --> 00:13:05.250
That's the objective of this expedition.

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:07.480
This hogwash is the objective ?

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:10.370
What kind of strategic
objectives are they trying to fulfill...

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:14.350
...by mobilizing several thousand ships,
sending several million soldiers to battle...

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:17.950
...and consuming exorbitant 
amounts of resources and energy ?

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:19.700
What good does it do to divert
the focus from the fundamentals...

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:25.270
...limiting assignments at a tactical level and discussing it{i.e. tactical assignment} with a pretense of authority ?

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:28.270
They're just playing
around at war games.

00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:33.600
They're truly suitable rivals for those idiots who
call themselves the Free Planets Alliance Fleet.

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:36.390
Or what ?

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:38.400
Considering the number of people defeated in power struggles within the Empire...

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:40.350
...many of which ended up
defecting to the Alliance...

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:43.250
...could it be conceivable that
they're going easy on the enemy...

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:45.750
{i.e. Alliance}...so as not to lose a place for
them to defect to in the future ?

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:48.350
No, I'm overestimating them.

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:51.090
Even with their maximum efforts, this is the best they could do.

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:55.100
Vice Admiral Musel, did you
have something to say ?

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:02.600
Even if you ask for an
opinion, I have none.

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:04.400
An {in ?}inexperienced person like myself...

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:09.240
...cannot match the thoughtfulness
of my lord Fleet Admiral, Sir.

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:12.950
Since it seems
there's no other input...

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:15.860
...we'll open a bottle of champagne to celebrate our victory in advance.

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:20.810
Let us toast to the glory of the
Kaiser and the prosperity of the Empire.

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:34.500
The mindset that 
assures them of victory...

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:38.600
...despite the fact that they haven't
done what is necessary is beyond me.

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:42.950
Then...

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:47.630
For the glory of the Kaiser !

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:50.220
For the glory of the Kaiser !

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:57.700
The three Alliance fleets 
that were sent ahead...

00:14:57.700 --> 00:15:00.180
...had already been deployed
in the Tiamat Starzone.

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:03.840
But the Chief Commander, Fleet 
Admiral Lobos, was still at the rear.

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:05.700
It was partly because the mobilization of the two rear-guard fleets...

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:10.710
...was not approved by the Ministry of Defense and their composition was not yet set.

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:13.600
Since the Chief Commander isn't here...

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:19.160
...logically, shouldn't Vice Admiral Bucock, as senior admiral, assume command ?

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:26.130
I understand, but I don't want any unnecessary interference with my fleet's activities.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:30.030
If you force me into contrived
coordination with other fleets...

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:33.630
...it will only kill my fleet's strength, and in the end, benefit the enemy.

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:36.810
We'll only be limiting our strategic options.

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:42.380
We have no strategic-level
choice to begin with.

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:45.300
The opposition will attack,
and we'll defend.

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:47.950
Like the Battle of Dagon Starzone...

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:51.420
...choosing the battleground to our advantage is just about all we can manage.

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:54.250
Are you satisfied just
being on the defensive ?

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.560
Aren't you ?

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:57.670
Of course not.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:16:01.700
As long as the spring of autocracy persists, we will continue to face threats forever...

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:04.810
...no matter how many times we thwart their invasions.

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:06.840
In order to end this 
war once and for all...

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:11.800
...we must make the long march to attack Odin, the source of all evil, and annihilate the Empire.

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:13.010
There's no other way.

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:18.660
But we don't even have the
power to seize Iserlohn Fortress.

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:24.840
It's even more impossible to travel 10,000 light years and invade the center of the Empire.

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:26.450
That's been the case up to now.

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:31.790
I respect your accomplishments
and experience, Admiral Bucock.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:35.300
I mean your past 
accomplishments and experience.

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:40.700
Commander, at the risk 
of being presumptuous...

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:44.110
...I wonder if our fleet should 
just strictly remain spectators...

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:47.950
...since Admiral Holland seems to be so confident in his plans.

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:53.240
Plans don't fail before
they're put into effect.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.530
According to my past
experience, that is.

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:01.710
On that same day, the Imperial fleet also invaded Tiamat Starzone.

00:17:01.710 --> 00:17:02.710
Enemy fleet confirmed.

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:04.060
Distance, 11 light seconds.

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:05.490
Fire !

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:13.700
From a formation without
an ounce of creativity...

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:16.830
...a battle without an ounce
of creativity is coming about.

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:20.700
It's a meaningless battle, but
if I commanded all the fleets...

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:23.650
...I could certainly 
engineer a one-sided victory.

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:25.500
Lord Reinhard.

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:28.590
Don't worry about it, Kircheis.

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:31.750
It's just a hobby, watching other people battle from the rear.

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:36.910
Besides, it might be for the best, depending on how we look at it.

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:42.100
It saves our combat potential, to be back here rather than to be thrust into the utmost front.

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:46.760
We could retain valuable combat potential
that could decide the outcome of the battle.

00:17:46.760 --> 00:17:48.350
I wonder if our Fleet Admiral is thinking the same way ?

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:53.010
No, the way Muckenberger
does things is always the same.

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:57.700
Just as he discounted and 
shelved the Grimmelshausen Fleet...

00:17:57.700 --> 00:18:00.810
...he considers my fleet
to be outside his plan.

00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:04.110
But regardless of 
the Fleet Admiral's plan...

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:08.890
...a scenario where our combat potential becomes the deciding factor might come about.

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:13.960
For that to happen, the enemy
should at least put up some effort.

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:15.400
That's right.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:17.090
And that would draw more attention.

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:20.450
If I make a significant contribution,
I will then become a full Admiral.

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:23.950
In that case, though this battle has no strategic value whatsoever...

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:27.760
...it would have some
political value for us.

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:35.600
All right ! All ships, charge !

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:38.270
But, Commander, if we 
do that, our formation will...

00:18:38.270 --> 00:18:39.220
That doesn't matter.

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:41.700
I'll show decrepit old 
people with inflexible brains...

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:45.790
...that lining up ships and exchanging 
crossfire isn't the only way to fight a battle !

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:49.150
One enemy fleet is charging us !

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:52.430
A convex attack ?
How impudent !

00:18:52.430 --> 00:18:53.840
Intercept them by focusing our fire !

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:12.910
Look at it !

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:16.540
This is the essence of the artistic 
fleet movement that I came up with !

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:25.360
Don't be flustered !

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:26.380
Spread out !

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:36.200
I don't know who the 
enemy commander is...

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:39.350
...but he seems to think that 
just ignoring theory is creative.

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:43.590
Of course, the side that's being
vexed by it is also truly pathetic.

00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:44.870
You're right.

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:47.700
But that fleet movement is artistic, isn't it ?

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:51.280
Then art is an unproductive thing.

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:53.650
Look at the disorderliness
of their movements.

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:57.150
It's like they're moving around just to waste their energy.

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:00.450
It's still creative, but...

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:06.560
Being creative means 
creating a new theory.

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:10.220
Destroying existing theory alone doesn't make someone creative.

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:13.380
Even though they're an enemy,
their tactics are truly praiseworthy.

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:19.560
The enemy commander's strategies
are beyond existing tactical theories.

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:21.700
Without having a set formation...

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:27.700
...they flow around like an amoeba in all
directions, and launch unexpected attacks.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:31.340
I must admit
he's exceptional.

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:34.630
There are always ones lower than
the low, you incompetent bastards.

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:38.950
Even if you were attacked unexpectedly, what's flustering you so ?

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:41.300
It's not like they were hit
in the heart of the fleet.

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:43.560
You say they're incompetent...

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:48.000
...but they're fighting bravely and fulfilling their duties as Imperial soldiers.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:53.660
On the other hand we're just watching the hard battle fought by our friendly units - what do you think, sir ?

00:20:55.680 --> 00:21:00.150
Looking at the enemy fleet, it's obvious that even though they're speedy and active...

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:02.250
...they're not coordinated 
with the other fleets...

00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:05.690
...and are ignoring the fact that
their supply line is over-extended.

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:09.200
In other words, they intend to 
wage an extreme, short-term battle.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:12.950
By employing a movement that ignores tactical basics, they intend to lead us into confusion...

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:16.320
...and multiply our casualties by
attacking while we're in disarray.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:19.950
In that case, we should avoid
engaging in the battle unnecessarily.

00:21:19.950 --> 00:21:22.250
When they charge, we should retreat the same distance...

00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:26.070
...and wait till their resources are
exhausted before we counterattack.

00:21:26.070 --> 00:21:30.080
Therefore, there's no reason to
engage in battle at present time.

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:32.300
Then when do we fight back ?

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:36.050
When the enemy reaches
the limit of its activities.

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:38.110
Oh, when will that be ?

00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:39.160
Will it be a year later ?

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:41.150
Or a hundred years later ?

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:01.600
Kircheis.

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:06.050
Kircheis, praise me.

00:22:06.050 --> 00:22:09.830
Really, it's remarkable how much
I've put up with these last two weeks.

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:13.170
I feel like I'm using up a
lifetime's supply of patience here.

00:22:14.240 --> 00:22:16.600
If you can be patient just
a little longer, you'll be fine.

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:23.070
If the situation turns around through your tactics, even an idiot will see who was right.

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:25.990
And at that point, you can
gloat as much as you wish.

00:22:28.010 --> 00:22:29.690
Let's do that.

00:22:29.690 --> 00:22:34.840
But, Kircheis, when I actually
do gloat, this is what you'll say:

00:22:34.840 --> 00:22:38.300
"They now realize their misdeeds and are ashamed of them..."

00:22:38.300 --> 00:22:40.700
"...so you should forgive them."

00:22:42.100 --> 00:22:45.600
You're kind, but I'll tell you this:

00:22:45.600 --> 00:22:48.970
You don't have to be kind to 
anyone else but me and my sister.

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:52.030
You don't have to 
treat others so kindly.

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:58.250
The battle, which will later be 
called the Third Battle of Tiamat...

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:02.460
...appeared to be headed for stagnation and was in the midst of a fierce exchange of fire.

00:23:00.650 --> 00:23:04.550
